cast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Eugene Vindman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 7th District pits first-term Democratic incumbent Eugene Vindman against Republican Doug Ollivant, a first-time congressional candidate who won a contested primary in August. The district leans Democratic by about two points, and the midterm environment adds to that tilt. No public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets.\n\nVindman has raised over $12 million and holds $6.6 million on hand, dwarfing Ollivant's roughly $250,000 war chest, with essentially no outside spending on either side. Ratings from ten outlets cluster at Likely D or better, and prediction markets give Vindman a 94-96 percent chance of winning. The forecast places him comfortably ahead, with residual uncertainty reflecting the lack of polling and typical midterm volatility.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 13.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9562, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9406, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9637, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9667, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9827, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9746, "margin": 12.5}]}